@1 = ~If you came to kill me, have at it. I've been patient for long enough. I don't want to live in captivity anymore. All I crave are the cold clutches of death.~
@2 = ~(kill the manticore)~
@3 = ~(Spare the manticore)~
@4 = ~Stop right there. Take one more step and I'll see how far these chains stretch. I might just be able to reach your throat, snack.~
@5 = ~What... what kind of creature are you?~
@6 = ~You're the one in chains. I don't think you'll be doing much.~
@7 = ~Centuries ago, during the heights of the ancient elven city, elven arcanists captured me when I was still a cub. They brought me down to this subterranean laboratory to study the innate magical properties. Putting me on display is more like it.~
@8 = ~What is the point of these tunnels?~
@9 = ~Can we help you in any way?~
@10 = ~So be it, snack. If I had at least a little more energy, I would consume you whole for this insult. Calling you selfish would be out of place, since I am no better than that. Leave me to my suffering. Just go.~
@11 = ~(kill the manticore)~
@12 = ~(Spare the manticore)~
@13 = ~(You slowly approach the manticore. A tense mix of sadness and relief shapes his ancient eyes. His magically prolonged life is finally coming to an end. Shifting his weight, the beast positions himself deliberately, exposing his chest for a clean kill. You take a deep breath. With one swift, heavy thrust, you pierce the creature straight through the heart. He lets out a final, stunted roar before his strength gives out. The collapse of his gargantuan body strikes the floor with a massive tremor, rattling the stone so violently you feel as if the entire dungeon might cave in right on your head. Then, the dust settles.

The manticore lies dead. He finally got what he wanted.)~
@14 = ~Haven't seen my kind before, have you? You humans would call us manticores. We are apex predators, and exceptionally deadly hunters. If not for these chains you'd find out the truth behind my words, snack.~
@15 = ~Be cautious, <CHARNAME>. Manticores are known to be highly dangerous predators. Keep thy distance and don't engage overmuch.~
@16 = ~By Tempus. Stories about large creatures I've been told as a child don't even compare to this... hybrid. Manticores truly earned their reputation for looking malevolent and majestic at the same time. What a view.~
@17 = ~If wyverns pay so well, I wonder how much THAT wonder would fetch on the market? Though, it breaks my heart to admit I would feel shameful murdering such a rare beauty out of mere greed.~
@18 = ~By Helm's watchful gaze! A manticore. Beast as beautiful as it is deadly. Watch your step! It is chained but who knows how securely these chains hold him.~
@19 = ~A manticore? Here? (And to think these Westgate simpletons flee from what a Thayan child learns to leash before mastering the second circle!) Stand back, you simians! Do not damage the tail spikes; they fetch an excellent price from buyers who actually possess a modicum of arcane intellect.~
@20 = ~Wretched thing! Slay that beast immediately. He's a stain on nature's world. Nothing but a gross aberration.~
@21 = ~Truly, I always believed manticores are but a fiction. A mixture of childish imagination and local legends, but to actually see one... It's frightening.~
@22 = ~Be on your guard! The beast is cleverer than a standard predator, and its spikes carry a foul venom. Speak if you must but keep your distance.~
@23 = ~B-by the gods! How did th-this creature happen to be d-d-down here? If it breaks free, w-w-we have no c-chance of slaying it! I have heard terrible tales of its m-m-might.~
@24 = ~Tiax gave it some thought and decided this will be his mount once he makes the world his dominion. No one touches my future pet! This privilege is already taken in advance.~
@25 = ~Look at it! Look at the exquisite stitching of its spine! Oh, the elegant fusion of lion and man! Tell me, beast... does your human face feel the draft when you fly? Oh, you wait till I get my fingers on you!~
@26 = ~I wish I could say I'm surprised, but traveling with you has already taught me never to underestimate your knack for finding the completely bizarre.~
@27 = ~Manticores are known to be vicious, deadly apex hunters. Don't let their look fool you, my friend. They can swallow you whole within seconds if you drop your guard.~
@28 = ~How did it even manage to fit down into a narrow dungeon like this? It's absolutely massive!~
@29 = ~Do I arouse fear in you, snack? Such delicious feeling. I haven't had anyone sneak in here, aside from those kobolds stumbling upon my lair over and over. You're in luck, snack. I won't eat you. I don't need food.~
@30 = ~Wild magic in this area affects me to a remarkable extent. Hunger is something I haven't felt since I was a mere cub. I can't even remember what it feels like to be hungry. If I eat, I feel no taste, no joy, no saturation. Just... numbness.~
@31 = ~Why are you in chains?~
@32 = ~What is the point of these tunnels?~
@33 = ~Can we help you in any way?~
@34 = ~Yes. Fair observation. Elven iron doesn't break and even if it had, I'm three times the size of the narrow entrance of this place and I won't be able to leave. My fate is sealed since the moment I became forgotten.~
@35 = ~Be cautious, <CHARNAME>. Manticores are known to be highly dangerous predators. Keep thy distance and don't engage overmuch.~
@36 = ~By Tempus. Stories about large creatures I've been told as a child don't even compare to this... hybrid. Manticores truly earned their reputation for looking malevolent and majestic at the same time. What a view.~
@37 = ~If wyverns pay so well, I wonder how much THAT wonder would fetch on the market? Though, it breaks my heart to admit I would feel shameful murdering such a rare beauty out of mere greed.~
@38 = ~By Helm's watchful gaze! A manticore. Beast as beautiful as it is deadly. Watch your step! It is chained but who knows how securely these chains hold him.~
@39 = ~A manticore? Here? (And to think these Westgate simpletons flee from what a Thayan child learns to leash before mastering the second circle!) Stand back, you simians! Do not damage the tail spikes; they fetch an excellent price from buyers who actually possess a modicum of arcane intellect.~
