@45 = ~Look at it! Look at the exquisite stitching of its spine! Oh, the elegant fusion of lion and man! Tell me, beast... does your human face feel the draft when you fly? Oh, you wait till I get my fingers on you!~
@46 = ~I wish I could say I'm surprised, but traveling with you has already taught me never to underestimate your knack for finding the completely bizarre.~
@47 = ~Manticores are known to be vicious, deadly apex hunters. Don't let their look fool you, my friend. They can swallow you whole within seconds if you drop your guard.~
@48 = ~How did it even manage to fit down into a narrow dungeon like this? It's absolutely massive!~
@49 = ~Do I arouse fear in you, snack? Such delicious feeling. I haven't had anyone sneak in here, aside from those kobolds stumbling upon my lair over and over. You're in luck, snack. I won't eat you. I don't need food.~
@50 = ~Wild magic in this area affects me to a remarkable extent. Hunger is something I haven't felt since I was a mere cub. I can't even remember what it feels like to be hungry. If I eat, I feel no taste, no joy, no saturation. Just... numbness.~
@51 = ~Why are you in chains?~
@52 = ~What is the point of these tunnels?~
@53 = ~Can we help you in any way?~
@54 = ~When the massive sorcerous battle erupted, the settlement outside turned into dust. A rogue torrent of experimental energy slammed into these hallways. Instead of killing me, the raw magical energy bonded with me, transforming me into a living magical battery. I appear to be the reason this area is eternally afflicted with wild magic.~
@55 = ~My existence keeps this place alive, and keeps ME alive. The energy made me immortal but elves either all died or forgot about me. I remained down here - lonely, trapped and abandoned. They never came back to free me. I grew to my current, massive size and even if I broke free, I have no power to leave.~
@56 = ~What is the point of these tunnels?~
@57 = ~Can we help you in any way?~
@58 = ~Aren't you uneducated. Firewine elves have built a system of corridors beneath the bridge that acted as a drainage network. This structure's underground was flooded until the river dried out. Vaults also had other practical usage but are now derelict, just like anything else here.~
@59 = ~This level is bordering with Underdark beneath. Entryway to it is located north from here somewhere, although judging by the state of collapse all over this place, chances are that you'll gain no access, snack.~
@60 = ~Though I am hesitant to lend my ear unto this creature, it may be that he speaketh with a twisted sort of wisdom. Ancient tomes I did once peruse in distant Rashemen do discourse upon a hidden entrance to the Underdark, with deep tunnels reaching even unto Throrgar. Yet take heed, for these be but reported speculations of old, and not empiric evidence born of true sight.~
@61 = ~This place is nothing but a rotting tomb of my despair.~
@62 = ~Why are you in chains?~
@63 = ~Can we help you in any way?~
@64 = ~Freedom. I crave freedom.~
@65 = ~You aren't actually thinking about it, are you? We can't free a creature born of evil!~
@66 = ~I don't want the freedom of life. I lived plenty. I want the freedom of death. I'm sick of the dark, I'm sick of the damp, and I'm sick of being a prisoner. You have weapons. Put a blade through my heart and end it. I'm begging you.~
@67 = ~It's your call, <CHARNAME>. I urge you to think this through cautiously. However vile manticores are, forsaking a suffering creature to an endless misery is below our station, I trust.~
@68 = ~So, what say you?~
@69 = ~I won't leave you here. I shall abide by your wishes and end your life.~
@70 = ~I will not kill you. I'll leave you to your fate. Pray that someone else comes.~
@71 = ~I thank you, snack. Unlike my kind I have never claimed a life before. Perhaps that shall purify my soul before whatever happens to me after death. Hah, futile desires.~
@72 = ~Just... do it fast, please. I suffered enough and I lived in pain for so long. I don't want anymore of that. I just want peace... eternal peace and silence.~
@73 = ~Your meek heart is extraordinarily vomit-inducing.~
@74 = ~(kill the manticore)~
@75 = ~(Spare the manticore)~
